      "html": "<p>With Quickler, the person on the job answers questions in WhatsApp by text, voice note or photo. The AI then:</p><ul><li>hears the voice note, with the words of your trade taught to the transcriber</li><li>reads the photos and documents you send</li><li>sorts each answer into the right question</li><li>rebuilds the answers after the walk from the whole conversation, with three independent reads voting on what was said</li><li>writes the report in your own template, with your styles, headings and logo</li><li>lists each fault with its place and writes a to-do job for each</li></ul><p>Every fact still comes from the person on the job. Every name, number and identifier on a record has to come from something actually said, sent or photographed. Rules that must never be wrong, such as answering only Yes, No or N/A and leaving no question unanswered, are fixed in code. They are not left to the AI.</p><p>Why bother with that? AI works more like rolling a dice than flicking a light switch. The clearer you are, the better the odds. I made a short video on it: <a href=\"/features/why-ai-gets-things-wrong/\">why AI gets things wrong</a>.</p>"
