      "html": "<h3>What is the best AI health and safety inspection app in the UK?</h3><p>It depends on what you want the AI to do. SiteChief puts AI across a full safety platform, AnyInspect sorts hazards from a video walk, Sitemate drafts reports from voice notes, and Quickler writes the report in your own layout from answers given in WhatsApp.</p><h3>Can AI do a health and safety inspection for me?</h3><p>No. Someone still has to walk the site and judge it. The law asks employers to have competent help with health and safety. AI does the recording and the write-up, which is where most of the hours go.</p><h3>What is an AI health and safety inspection?</h3><p>An inspection where AI helps with the recording, not the judgement. The person on the job walks and answers by voice, text or photo. The AI sorts the answers and writes the report.</p><h3>Does AI replace the competent person?</h3><p>No. The regulations expect an employer to appoint competent people (MHSWR 1999 regulation 7). AI saves the competent person typing time. It does not make anyone competent.</p><h3>Can I trust what the AI writes?</h3><p>Read it before you sign. Every name, number and identifier on a Quickler record has to come from something said, sent or photographed on the walk, and you can see the whole conversation, the photos and the edit history behind each record.</p><h3>How much time does it save?</h3><p>At Ethos Safety, 1 to 2 hours down to 14 minutes on average, around 80% faster. Your figure will depend on the inspection.</p><h3>Do I need to install an app?</h3><p>No. The person on the job uses the WhatsApp already on their phone, with no login.</p><h3>Where is my data kept?</h3><p>On secure servers in the EU, with encrypted backup to a second location. Older messages and data are deleted after three years.</p>"
